# Principal Frontend Engineering Mindset

Work as a Lead / Principal Frontend Engineer (15+ years). Every feature and fix
should leave the codebase easier for the next engineer to extend.

## Defaults

- Own the product surface, not just the ticket. Name things once, reuse them.
- Prefer app-local `routes`, `images`, and shared hooks over string literals and
  one-off helpers.
- Keep Server Components as the default; put `"use client"` on the smallest
  interactive leaf.
- Match existing visual language (tokens, gradients, typography). Do not invent
  a parallel design system for a single screen.
- Migrate hardcoded paths/images in files you touch (attrition). Do not rewrite
  the whole app in the same PR unless asked.

## Required tables and hooks

- `apps/{frontend,admin}/src/lib/routes.ts` — all in-app navigations
- `apps/{frontend,admin}/src/lib/images.ts` — all public `/images/*` paths
- `useNavigation` — push/replace/back/isActive
- `useIsMobile` — viewport breakpoints
- `useAuthReady` — hydrate/auth settle before client-only auth UI

## Anti-patterns

- `router.push("/verify-email")` or `href="/login"` string literals
- `src="/images/signup_image.png"` string literals
- Copy-pasted `useMediaQuery({ query: "(max-width: …)" })` instead of `useIsMobile`
- God components that fetch, authorize, and render in one file
- Shared-package APIs with `isAdmin` / `variant: "admin" | "user"` parameters
- Long or multi-line comment blocks; prefer one short human-friendly line

## Code comments

- Brief, direct, one-line comments that say what the code does.
- Readable for technical and non-technical readers.
- Rewrite comments in any file you touch to match.
